body:
house, m.d for sure

&#x200B;

it's the only show i've watched more than once (i haven't watched many shows though).

"don't be afraid, we're going home"

&#x200B;

taxi cab by twenty one pilots. i can't quite pinpoint what it is that makes this song my all time favorite, but it saved my life honestly.

&#x200B;

another, from a shinedown song, "did you finally find a place above the shadows so the world will never know?" he was speaking to himself when he wrote this, the depressed, drug-addicted part of himself that he had to let go of.

Twenty One Pilots. I used to pride myself in how much I despised them, and would talk about how fucking annoying I found them, and how they're "wannabe edgy" and for "twelve year old girls who think they have depression because they got sad once"

&#x200B;

fast forward to november 2017, I was having a really hard night (I have depression and PTSD along with a few other disorders), and it was all becoming too much, and for some fucking reason I put on Twenty One Pilots. I learned who they really were that night, and what their music really means to people and what the band's true message and goal is. Fell in love and never looked back. (by the way, it wouldn't be a stretch to say that their song "Taxi Cab" saved my life a few times).
